title: The Generals Move
subtitle: Troops march on the capital.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: opp_gen_ev = 2 and dix >= 6
priority: 26
on-arrival: {!
Q.opp_gen_ev = 0;
Q.opp_gen_timer = 8;
Q.opp_gen_n = (Q.opp_gen_n || 0) + 1;
Q.opp_why = RO.mainGrievance(Q, 'gen');
Q.opp_bonus = 0;
!}

= The Generals Move

Having failed to change [+ opp_why +] by memorandum, the generals have decided to do it by other means. Two cavalry divisions and a number of shock battalions are moving on Petrograd and Moscow, "to restore order". Their officers have promised the Kadets that no one will be hanged unless they deserve it.

The railwaymen's union is divided, and the garrisons are doubtful. How should the democracy meet the generals?

- @committees: Form a committee for the defence of the revolution, with the Bolsheviks.
- @railways: Call on the railwaymen and the Soviet to stop the trains.
- @loyal: Rely on the garrisons that have stayed loyal.

@committees
choose-if: rel_bol >= 20
unavailable-subtitle: The Bolsheviks will not help us.
on-arrival: {!
Q.opp_bonus = 14;
Q.bol_armed = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 8, bolshevik: 10});
!}

The committee was formed in a night, and the Bolshevik leaders sat on it with the others. Workers were armed from the arsenals, and agitators were sent to meet the troops.

- @coup_result: Continue...

@railways
on-arrival: {!
Q.opp_bonus = 10;
RO.add(Q, {soviet_democracy: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {railway: 3});
!}

The railwaymen's executive ordered that no train carry troops against the Soviet, and the stationmasters, for once, obeyed. Soviet agitators went out to meet the troops on every siding.

- @coup_result: Continue...

@loyal
on-arrival: {!
Q.opp_bonus = 5;
RO.add(Q, {army_discipline: 2});
!}

The government telegraphed to the garrisons that it was still the government. Most of them replied that it was.

- @coup_result: Continue...

@coup_result
on-arrival: {!
Q.opp_force = RO.kornilovForce(Q) + (Q.ant_gen - 70) / 4;
Q.opp_resist = RO.kornilovResistance(Q, Q.opp_bonus);
Q.opp_win = Q.opp_force > Q.opp_resist ? 0 : 1;
if (Q.opp_win) {
    RO.add(Q, {ant_gen: -40, right_threat: -18, army_discipline: -4, soviet_democracy: 3});
    RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 1, workers: 1});
} else {
    Q.game_end = 1;
    Q.ending = 'right_coup';
}
!}
go-to: coup_defeated if opp_win = 1; coup_won if opp_win = 0

@coup_defeated

The divisions stopped at a siding outside the capital, and their men would not go further. Their generals were arrested by their own officers, or fled. It was a victory, and the army has not recovered from it. The generals have nothing left to ask, and nothing left to hope for.

@coup_won

The committees were too few and the troops too many. On a night in the autumn the generals took the capital and dissolved the Soviets. The Assembly has been told to adjourn. General Alexeyev has declared a military dictatorship.

The party's leaders have been arrested, or have fled abroad.
